@startuml bootstrap-sequence
!include _style.puml

title Qt client — bootstrap sequence

autonumber

actor "User" as User $external
participant "main (app/qt or app/wt)" as Main $tier
participant "ClientApplication" as App $tier
participant "CoreModule" as Core $tier
participant "LoginDialog" as Login $tier
participant "Backend" as Backend $external
participant "Profile" as Profile $store
participant "Domain modules" as Modules $tier
participant "MainWindowModule" as MW $tier

User -> Main : launch client.exe
Main -> Main : parse command line, install translator
Main -> App : new ClientApplication(ctx)
activate App
App -> Core : new CoreModule(executor)
Core --> App : tracer, command registries, progress host
note right of App : also: transport_factory_, master_data_services_
deactivate App

Main -> App : Start()
activate App
App -> Login : login_handler_(ctx)
activate Login
Login -> User : prompt credentials and backend
User --> Login : username, password, backend
Login -> Backend : connect and authenticate
Backend --> Login : services
Login --> App : DataServices
deactivate Login

App -> App : PostLogin()
App -> Profile : Load()
Profile --> App : window layouts, pages, prefs

group Construct domain modules in dependency order
  App -> Modules : EventModule, TimedDataService, TaskManager,\nConnectionStateReporter, WriteService
  App -> Modules : ConfigurationModule, DebuggerModule, FileSystemComponent
  App -> Modules : FavoritesModule, PortfolioModule
  App -> Modules : ModusModule, VidiconModule (Qt only)
  App -> Modules : ExportConfigurationModule
end

App -> MW : new MainWindowModule(ctx)
activate MW
MW -> Profile : read pages and window definitions
MW -> MW : instantiate views via ControllerRegistry
MW -> User : display main window
deactivate MW
deactivate App

note over User, MW
  After bootstrap the UI is live — events stream in via EventFetcher
  and values via the monitored-item subscription
end note

@enduml
